---
import LegalPage from '../layouts/LegalPage.astro';
import Fill from '../components/Fill.astro';
import { OWNER } from '../config/legal';
---

<LegalPage
  title="About us"
  description="Who runs B2BRated, how the site is paid for and who signs off the pages."
  path="/about"
>
  <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
  <p>
    B2BRated is run by <Fill value={OWNER.legalName} label="legal name" />, based in
    <Fill value={OWNER.country} label="country" />. Postal address for legal notices:
    <Fill value={OWNER.address} label="address" />. You can reach us at <Fill value={OWNER.email} label="contact email" />.
  </p>

  <h2>What the site is for</h2>
  <p>
    We compare business software by category. For each product we publish the plan prices, what each plan includes,
    security and contract terms where the vendor states them, and a link to the vendor page each figure came from. The
    <a href="/methodology">methodology page</a> explains how a product earns a place in a category.
  </p>

  <h2>Who writes and checks the pages</h2>
  <p>
    Category pages are drafted with AI assistance and checked against the vendors' own pages. Each page will be signed
    off by <Fill value={OWNER.editor} label="editor name" /> before it is treated as final. A sign-off means the editor
    approved the inclusion criteria and the copy. It does not mean the editor has used every product.
  </p>

  <h2>How the site is paid for</h2>
  <p>
    Today the owner pays for it and it earns nothing. No vendor pays us, and there are no affiliate links or ads. We
    expect to charge vendors for tools such as claimed profiles, lead requests and clearly labelled sponsored
    placements. We will describe each paid product on the <a href="/advertising-disclosure">advertising and
    sponsorship page</a> before the first payment, and the rules on that page will apply from the start.
  </p>

  <h2>Reviews</h2>
  <p>
    Review collection has not opened. There are no reviews on the site and no scores. When reviews open, the
    <a href="/review-guidelines">review guidelines</a> apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Mistakes</h2>
  <p>
    If something on a page is wrong, tell us on the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> and include a link to a public
    page that shows the correct fact.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
